{
  // Type-check program for the build/tooling suite. vitest runs these files
  // through esbuild transpile-only, so without this gate every type-level
  // contract in test/build (the `@ts-expect-error` pins on the untyped .mjs
  // imports, the workflow/SBOM parsing helpers) is erased and never enforced.
  //
  // These tests exercise the BUILD side of the repo — esbuild configs, the
  // scripts/ tooling, the packaged workflow YAML — so the compiler view is
  // Node + ESM, with no DOM lib and no vscode-webview types.
  //
  // The scripts/ and esbuild.config.mjs modules they import are plain .mjs with
  // no bundled types. Every one of those imports carries a line-scoped
  // `@ts-expect-error` on the module specifier — it self-verifies (goes red the
  // day the module gains types) and leaves everything the test itself authors
  // checked. As of 2026-08-28 no file here uses a file-level `@ts-nocheck`,
  // which would switch the WHOLE file off and make any type-level assertion in
  // it vacuous; five suites sat in that state from the day this config landed
  // (2026-08-22) until the swap.
  //
  // ⚠️ When a wrapping binding list would push the specifier off the directive's
  // line, use a namespace import and destructure below — a wrapped named import
  // silently unsuppresses (theme-palettes.test.ts documents the measurement).
  //
  // The tripwire against drifting back is no-file-level-ts-nocheck.test.ts, and
  // it is the AUTHORITY — its accept/reject sets were measured against this
  // repo's own tsc (5.9.3) by planting a type error behind each directive form
  // and watching whether tsc suppressed it. It scans recursively and asks
  // TypeScript itself whether each file is opted out, rather than matching
  // patterns in the text — and it decodes each file the way `sys.readFile`
  // does (UTF-8 BOM stripped, UTF-16LE/BE decoded), because an oracle is only
  // faithful when it is fed the same string tsc reads.
  // ⚠️ Asking is not over-engineering — it is what three hand-rolled
  // approximations failed at during this file's own review, each one measured
  // only after it shipped: a whole-file block-comment strip that swallowed live
  // directives, a leading-trivia walk that stopped at a shebang, and a
  // whitespace class that missed U+0085 and U+200B. Every miss pointed the same
  // dangerous way — file reported clean, checking actually off. Run
  // `pnpm vitest run test/build/no-file-level-ts-nocheck.test.ts`.
  //
  // For a quick eyeball there is
  // `git grep -ilE '^[[:space:]]*///?[[:space:]]*@ts-nocheck([[:space:]]|:|$)' test/build`,
  // but treat it as an APPROXIMATION, not a second authority. What `[[:space:]]`
  // covers depends on the grep build and the locale — on this machine's BSD grep
  // it matched form feed, vertical tab and NBSP but not U+0085 or U+200B, and a
  // GNU grep elsewhere need not agree — so the classes the test pins are exactly
  // what a one-liner cannot promise. It also has no way to model block-comment
  // trivia or a shebang, and it reads bytes as text, so a UTF-16 file is
  // invisible to it. It is anchored per line for the same reason the test is —
  // this header names the directive in prose repeatedly, and the unanchored
  // `git grep -l '@ts-nocheck' test/build` still hits it.
  //
  // noEmit (inherited): this is a CI gate, not a build step — vitest still runs
  // through its own transpiler. rootDir is pinned to the repo root explicitly
  // (matching the sibling test tsconfigs) so the program's containment boundary
  // is stated rather than inferred — the ../../src/shared files sit outside
  // test/build/, and an inferred rootDir would silently widen with the include.
  // It plays no part in resolving that cross-layer import: rootDir governs emit
  // layout and the TS6059 containment check only, never module resolution.
  "extends": "../../tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "module": "esnext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "lib": ["es2022"],
    "types": ["node"],
    "rootDir": "../.."
  },
  "include": ["**/*.ts", "../../src/shared/**/*.ts"]
}
